  <h3>How many words on a line?</h3>
  <p>Between 3 and 10 words. 10 is best for single blocks</p>
  <h3>Text size</h3>
  <p>never go below 16px = 1rem. And line distance is 1.4</p>
  <h3>Clear media queries</h3>
  <p>always nest media queries so your css is easy to read</p>
  <h3>for select option styling</h3>
  <p>
    you can style select box and the option fully via appearance base select.
    this is not compatible everywhere tho
  </p>
  <h3>Don't get held back</h3>
  <p>
    Don't let compatibility hold you back to make the site be the best it can be.
  </p>
  <h3>Three properties of clear readable text</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Size 1 rem</li>
    <li>line height 1.4</li>
    <li>3 to 10 words on a line</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Was Josef Müller-Brock right?</h3>
  <p>Yes</p>
  <h3>Looking back to day 1 till 15</h3>
  <p>A bunch of things about responsive design</p>
  <h3>What are the best steps to take to design mobile first</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Use devtools to look at your html at mobile size</li>
    <li>style the website for that size</li>
    <li>use devtools to make your website wider until it's ugly</li>
    <li>
      use units that are relative to the size of the viewport and media queries
      at the ugly breakpoints
    </li>
  </ol>
  <h3>what is vmin?</h3>
  <p>Represents in percentage the smallest of vw and vh</p>
  <h3>Rule one of Aria</h3>
  <p>Don't use aria, good html will do the correct accessibility</p>
  <h3>Aria problem</h3>
  <p>aria doesn't translate well</p>
  <h3>Use Alt</h3>
  <p>
    Alt for images with a purpose must have an alt text describing the
    function. if it doesn't have a function or it's just fluff. alt=" "
  </p>
  <h3>Svgs with alt?</h3>
  <p>Svg doesn't use alt. use title for the function if it has one</p>
  <h3>Declarative partial templates</h3>
  <p>injecting code templates on the client side as html only</p>
